<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 235 0 R
/T (The RNA fragments are known to be fragile and the slightest difference in how a sample is handled can leave its mark. The field is so young that no cfRNA clock has been built yet. However, transcriptomic clocks already succeed on tissue and blood RNA and cfRNA itself is already used to detect diseases, proof that it carries rich biological information. )
/E (The RNA fragments are known to be fragile and the slightest difference in how a sample is handled can leave its mark. The field is so young that no cfRNA clock has been built yet. However, transcriptomic clocks already succeed on tissue and blood RNA and cfRNA itself is already used to detect diseases, proof that it carries rich biological information. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
