/T (Flomics applies strict quality control at every step. Plasma is double-spun and checked for haemolysis, old samples are excluded, and DNA is removed during RNA extraction. Each sequenced sample must pass thresholds on exonic reads, spliced reads and library diversity. Even with these checks, residual platelets remain one of the main sources of variation in cell-free RNA.)
