/T (To mitigate potential unit-specific biases, we ultimately retained genes whose correlation with age was consistent across care units, aiming to reduce the influence of unit-dependent effects by prioritizing genes that exhibit a stable association with age across different settings. However, this selection strategy has important limitations: it is based on statistical consistency rather than biological relevance and may therefore exclude genes with genuine age-related effects that vary across populations or clinical settings. Given the limited number of care units available, the estimated consistency may not generalize to different settings.)
/E (To mitigate potential unit-specific biases, we ultimately retained genes whose correlation with age was consistent across care units, aiming to reduce the influence of unit-dependent effects by prioritizing genes that exhibit a stable association with age across different settings. However, this selection strategy has important limitations: it is based on statistical consistency rather than biological relevance and may therefore exclude genes with genuine age-related effects that vary across populations or clinical settings. Given the limited number of care units available, the estimated consistency may not generalize to different settings.)
