674 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 252 0 R
/E (This internship started from an exciting idea: could a single blood draw reveal how fast our body is really ageing? The goal was to build a model that captures ageing and stays interpretable, so that beyond a number, it tells us something about the biology behind it. Every step pushed in that direction. We made sure the signal reflects ageing rather than how samples were collected, linked genes to real biological functions, and designed an evaluation that leads the model to learn what all patients share as they age. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
675 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 252 0 R
/E (And the promise of this work is worth it: help moving medicine from treating diseases once they appear toward preventing them.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
