/Title (To assess the biological relevance of the identified gene modules, we performed enrichment analyses using two complementary databases: Gene Ontology \(GO\), which provides information on gene functions and biological processes, and the Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes \(KEGG\), which describes functional pathways. A function or pathway was considered enriched when a module contained more genes associated with it than expected by chance.)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1560 0 R
/Next 1786 0 R
>>
endobj
1706 0 obj
<<
/Title (Based on these criteria, the red module \(271 genes\), associated with the inflammatory response, emerged as a biologically relevant candidate, given the well-established relationship between ageing and chronic, low-grade inflammation.)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1560 0 R
/Prev 1787 0 R
>>
